 "key": "G major",
 "meter": "4/4",
 "bpm": 104,
 "about": "Friction from the grip of a chappal down to atoms, out to the tides slowing the Earth, and the open question of why ice is slippery.",
 "sections": [
  {
   "name": "Verse",
   "lines": [
    "Hand & hand,",
    "Shoe & ground,",
    "Wherever two things meet,",
    "A grip is found;",
    "Look up close,",
    "The smoothest floor",
    "Is hills and dips",
    "And mountains more;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Verse 2",
   "lines": [
    "Peak by peak",
    "They catch and hold,",
    "Atom tugging atom,",
    "Brave and bold;",
    "Snap and slide,",
    "And snap again,",
    "Every snap a little warmth",
    "Left in the grain."
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Chorus",
   "lines": [
    "Friction! Oh Friction!",
    "Are you friend or foe?",
    "You hold my feet upon the road,",
    "But slow me as I go!",
    "You wear the temple steps away,",
    "You stop the rolling ball,",
    "But without you could I hold a hand?",
    "Could I stand at all?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Verse 3",
   "lines": [
    "The water-pourer knew,",
    "Out on the desert sand,",
    "Just damp enough, the sledge would glide",
    "Across the land;",
    "And far out in the sea,",
    "The tides rub on the floor,",
    "Slowing down our spinning Earth,",
    "Each day a little more."
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Bridge",
   "lines": [
    "Even ice, so slippery,",
    "Keeps a secret still:",
    "Why it slides, nobody knows,",
    "Maybe one day you will."
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Chorus",
   "lines": [
    "Friction! Oh Friction!",
    "Are you friend or foe?",
    "You hold my feet upon the road,",
    "But slow me as I go!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Outro",
   "lines": [
    "Friction! Oh Friction!",
    "Rough & smooth & fine,",
    "Holding on to all we touch,",
    "Through space & time,",
    "Friction..."
   ]
  }
